{"kind":"assert","text":"Self-host requests: review and order (27 October). Three requests to the planner: the SeaweedFS record 373596467, the load findings a6847815 and the launchd and HTTPS findings e6a5cd22. This ruling decides each item and the order; the filings named here rest on the requests they answer.\n\nOrder. The first local deployment is the current direction, so its blockers go ahead of plan 033's remaining slice G4 and the standing release items. H1's condition \"never ahead of the grow demo slices\" is lifted (amendment on 99918e60). Builder queue, in order: the R14 documents child (filed; small; the builder is recutting it); the census f51f16f4 (promised, decisions answered); G1 host none; H1 amended; LAN address keys; CLI sessions and verify; uniqueness by index; idle alarms. Planner work: the SeaweedFS record reviewed today; the self-hosting note's next draft after G1; G2 after G1 carries the kit parameters and trust steps; H3 after H1 carries the launchd and Caddy settings.\n\nBlockers of a usable local deployment:\n- e6a5cd22 item 2, http:// behind the proxy: H1, as a configured public origin setting; no forwarded header is trusted for identity.\n- e6a5cd22 item 3, rate-limit keys: its own slice. Link-local and unique-local IPv6 keyed by the full address; the bearer-failure counter keyed by addressKey.\n- e6a5cd22 item 6 (room creation needs the demo offer) and a6847815 item 6 (creation admission needs ARTIFACTS_CONFIG off Cloudflare): G1, with a host-independent register setting.\n- e6a5cd22 item 1, the head stream on celld: a celld matter, with no dap fallback. The stream is one ReadableStream returned over the object RPC and relayed (packages/scope/src/worker.ts:233-246, sessions.ts:549); a polling second transport kept for one runtime is the kind of cost the sprint reports now review. Until celld carries streams across isolates, self-hosted readers poll history as the CLI does. The page has no live updates on any host today (apps/room/page/src uses no stream): that is the member and presence UI work of note 9554919b, not a self-host item.\n\nLimits under load (a6847815):\n- item 1, about 1,000 members: uniqueness guards answered from an index over fixed slots; slice filed.\n- item 2 and e6a5cd22 item 5, the session cap: the cap stays; the CLI reuses its session, reports 429 as rate-limited and falls back to signed reads only on forbidden; in the CLI slice.\n- item 3, verify --all: pages under a budget instead of 64 scopes, reads the register through the membership session's chained reads, and founding on an open register must not need a prior signed read; in the CLI slice.\n- item 4, idle cost: an investigation slice with a witness that quiescent scopes hold no alarm; a celld matter if dap arms none.\n- item 5: the self-hosting note's next draft (planner): a single-node case for section 4.7's drain check; the 60 s waker scan.\n\nLaunchd and HTTPS (e6a5cd22):\n- item 4, shutdown order: H3's kit makes the store outlive celld (the celld unit depends on the store's), and celld skipping the handoff as the only node is a celld matter.\n- item 6: set-role NaN and the \"outcome unknown\" wording in the CLI slice; /health 503 is the stand-in entry and goes with H1's real project.\n- the kit parameters (KeepAlive, run as the user, ExitTimeOut 60, ThrottleInterval 70, start after a store PUT, Caddy grace_period 10s, the served Caddyfile, the certificate profile, authenticated restart) go to H3; the trust steps and the certificate profile to G2.\n\ncelld matters (dap does nothing for them; for Hugh to carry): RPC streams across isolate boundaries for a ReadableStream returned from an object method; a single-node drain that never seals, and the handoff with the store already gone; the 60 s waker scan (a timed rule 20.2 s late); restoring cells with no request, if the alarm witness clears dap.\n\nNot changed: SeaweedFS stays the local bucket as recorded; no dap change for the store's three configuration findings."}